msgid "Show the gallery on listing pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:72
msgid "Adds a Gallery section to the foot of every listing by that vendor, before the reviews. Vendors with no gallery get no section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:78
msgid "Gallery Button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:79
msgid "Show the photo count on the View Gallery button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:80
msgid "With this off, the sidebar button simply reads \"View Gallery\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:105
msgid "Gallery Button Position (Vendor Pages)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:106
msgid "Where the View Gallery button sits in a vendor profile sidebar. Leave empty to group it with the action buttons beside Send Message, which suits most sites. Enter a number for a place of its own; lower sits higher. The summary card is 10, details 20, social links 25 and action buttons 30, so 24 sits just above social links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:114
msgid "Gallery Button Position (Listing Pages)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:115
msgid "The same choice for listing pages, which are numbered differently. Leave empty to group the button with the action buttons. The details are 10, social links 15, action buttons 20 and the vendor card 30, so 14 sits just above social links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:123
msgid "Maximum Folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:124
msgid "Set the maximum number of gallery folders per vendor. Leave empty for no limit. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:131
msgid "Maximum Images per Folder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:132
msgid "Set the maximum number of images allowed in each folder. Leave empty for the default of 30. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:139
msgid "Videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:140
msgid "Allow uploading videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:146
msgid "Likes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:147
msgid "Let visitors like individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:148
msgid "Adds a heart button with a public count to every photo. Only signed-in visitors can like, once per photo."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:155
msgid "AI Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:156
msgid "Review the first ten photos in each folder with AI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:157
msgid "Checks a folder's photos with the free OpenAI Moderation endpoint when the vendor saves the folder, using the API key from the Integrations settings. Each save reviews up to ten photos not reviewed before; set the photo limit below to guarantee full coverage. OpenAI fetches each photo from your site, so only public folders on a publicly reachable site can be checked, and when the service is unavailable saving simply proceeds unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:171
msgid "AI Moderation Photo Limit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:172
msgid "Cap each folder at this many photos, from 1 to 10, so one review covers the whole folder. Overrides higher limits, including per-plan ones. Folders already over the cap keep their photos but cannot take new ones. Leave empty for no cap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:181
msgid "Comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:182
msgid "Let visitors comment on individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:183
msgid "Every photo gets its own page with a comment thread, where signed-in visitors can comment, reply and like comments. People can delete their own comments, and the folder owner can delete any comment on their photos."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:190
msgid "Protect Files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:191
msgid "Protect private and members-only image files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:192
msgid "Moves private and members-only files out of the folder your web server publishes and serves them through an access-checked link, with unguessable names for new uploads. Recommended. If your hosting prevents the move, a notice above explains what to do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:199
msgid "Button Corner Rounding (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:200
msgid "Rounds the corners of every button this plugin adds, so they match your site. Leave empty to keep the theme's shape, which suits most sites. 0 is square; larger is rounder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:208
msgid "Maximum File Size (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:209
msgid "Reject gallery uploads larger than this many megabytes. Leave empty for no gallery-specific limit (the server upload limit still applies)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:216
msgid "Storage Limit (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:217
msgid "Cap the total disk space each vendor's gallery may use, including thumbnails. Vendors see their usage on their Gallery page. Leave empty for no cap. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:224
msgid "Allowed Image Formats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:225
msgid "Choose which image formats vendors may upload. Leave empty to allow all supported formats."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:239
msgid "Maximum Image Dimensions (pixels)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:240
msgid "Resize uploads so neither side exceeds this many pixels; around 2000 suits most galleries. Leave empty to keep the original dimensions. For compression, WebP conversion and bulk work on existing images, use a dedicated image plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:258
msgid "Gallery Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:259
msgid "How galleries look to visitors. These apply to the gallery page, to each folder page, and to the gallery sections you can add to vendor profiles and listing pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:264
msgid "Gallery Layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:265
msgid "Folder covers shows a grid of cover pictures, each opening the folder's own page. Single page puts every folder's photos on the gallery page one after another."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:271
msgid "Folder covers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:272
msgid "Single page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:277
msgid "Folder Columns"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:278
msgid "How many folder covers sit side by side on a full-width screen. Leave empty to fit as many as the screen allows. Narrow screens always show fewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:294
msgid "Maximum Rows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:295
msgid "Caps the folder grid in the Gallery sections on vendor profiles and listing pages, linking to the full gallery for the rest. Leave empty to show every folder. Needs a column count above. The gallery page itself always shows all folders, as it is the only route to them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:303
msgid "Cover Shape"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:304
msgid "The shape each folder cover is cropped to. Horizontal suits landscapes and interiors; vertical suits portraits and fashion. Choose the one your vendors mostly shoot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:310
msgid "Horizontal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:311
msgid "Vertical"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:312
msgid "Square"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:317
msgid "Lightbox"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:318
msgid "Let visitors enlarge the photo on its page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:319
msgid "With this on, clicking the photo on its own page enlarges it in a pop-up viewer. Photos in the gallery always open their own page, where the comments live."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:326
msgid "Gallery Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:327
msgid "Adds a sidebar to the gallery page, showing the vendor's profile card. You can add your own widgets to it in the \"Gallery Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:333
#: includes/configs/settings.php:347
msgid "No sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:334
#: includes/configs/settings.php:348
#: includes/configs/settings.php:373
msgid "Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:335
#: includes/configs/settings.php:349
#: includes/configs/settings.php:374
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:340
msgid "Folder Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:341
msgid "Adds a sidebar to each folder page, showing the vendor's profile card. You can add your own widgets to it in the \"Folder Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:366
msgid "Photo Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:367
msgid "Which side of the photo page the sidebar sits on. It holds the vendor's profile card and the owner's editing options, so it cannot be switched off. Add your own widgets in the \"Photo Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:381
msgid "Gallery Monetisation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:382
msgid "Members-only folders are how galleries make money: visitors must unlock them before seeing inside. <strong>To charge through memberships</strong>, add the gallery privileges to a paid HivePress Memberships plan, or to a free plan to simply require an account. <strong>To let vendors charge instead</strong>, enable paid access below: locked folders then offer that vendor's one-off purchase, falling back to your upgrade page link where no price is set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:387
msgid "Members-Only Folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:388
msgid "Let vendors mark folders as members-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:389
msgid "Members-only folders appear locked until a visitor gains access through a membership plan or a purchase. With this off, vendors choose only public or private, and existing members-only folders behave as private."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:402
msgid "Locked Folder Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:403
msgid "Choose how members-only folders appear to visitors without access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:409
msgid "Show blurred previews"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:410
msgid "Show locked placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:411
msgid "Hide completely"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:416
msgid "Paid Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:417
msgid "Let vendors sell access to their members-only folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:418
msgid "Vendors set their own prices and lengths, from a day to permanent, up to three offers at once. Buying is a normal WooCommerce checkout, so WooCommerce is required. While a vendor sells access, their locked folders show the purchase button rather than the upgrade page link. With HivePress Marketplace, these sales count towards vendor earnings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:436
msgid "What Access Buys"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:437
msgid "Whole gallery: one set of prices unlocks all of a vendor's members-only folders at once. Each folder separately: prices are set per folder and a buyer unlocks only the folder they paid for. Prices set under one choice are kept if you switch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:444
msgid "The vendor's whole gallery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:445
msgid "Each folder separately"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:450
msgid "Commission Rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:451
msgid "Your percentage of a gallery access sale, added at checkout as a separate Platform fee line, so the vendor still receives their price. Leave both commission boxes empty to take none. It only reaches you if your gateway settles gallery orders into the site's own account, which is the normal case; a gateway that charges each vendor's connected account directly pays the whole order to the vendor, so take your cut through that gateway instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:460
msgid "Commission Fee"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:461
msgid "A flat amount on top of the rate, charged once per gallery access sale. Use either box on its own or both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:468
msgid "Upgrade Page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:469
msgid "Choose the page locked visitors are sent to, e.g. your membership pricing page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:479
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:480
msgid "Your galleries are kept if you ever delete this plugin. WordPress's own warning that deleting a plugin also deletes its data is generic and does not describe this one: nothing is removed unless you tick the box first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:485
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:486
msgid "Delete folders, likes, comments and settings when this plugin is deleted (photos stay in your media library)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:487
msgid "Unticked, deleting the plugin keeps every folder, photo, like, comment, purchased access and setting, so reinstalling restores your galleries exactly. Ticked, deleting the plugin permanently removes all of that; photos always stay in your media library. This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

